We have derived improved differentiability properties for solutions to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
  \begin{equation*}
  \min\left\{\int_{\Omega}f\left(x,\mathbf{D}u\right)\,dx:\,u\in
  \mathcal{K}_\psi(\Omega)\right\}.
  \end{equation*}
  The kernel space $\mathcal{K}_\psi(\Omega)$ is defined by the condition
  \begin{equation*}
  \mathcal{K}_\psi(\Omega):=\Big\{\psi\leq u\in W^{1,p}(\Omega):\,
  \mathbf{D}\psi\in L^\infty(\Omega,\mathbb{R}^{n\times n})\Big\}.
  \end{equion*}
  The integral functional $\int_{\Omega}f\left(x,\mathbf{D}u\right)\,dx$ exhibits sub-quadratic growth with respect to the argument $\mathbf{D}u$.
  While existing literature has predominantly focused on obstacle problems with variational structure and quadratic growth conditions, this study addresses problems with sub-quadratic growth.
